  "topic": "Read and write Dha (emphatic) (ظ) at the beginning, middle and end of words, with Fatha, Kasra and Damma.",
  "minutes": 10,
  "learn": [
    {
      "en": "This is Dha (emphatic). Emphatic 'Th' — like the 'th' in 'that' but heavier and deeper. Very unique to Arabic!",
      "title": "Meet Dha (emphatic)!",
      "ar": "ظ",
      "aud": "c-0-ar",
      "tr": "Dha (emphatic)"
    },
    {
      "en": "Same shape as Ta (jug/vessel) but with a dot on top of the vertical stroke. Dha is Ta with a DOT on top — the emphatic version of Dhal. Deep and powerful!",
      "title": "How to write Dha (emphatic)"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a fatha, heavy Dha says “za”.",
      "title": "Dha (emphatic) with fatha",
      "ar": "ظَ",
      "aud": "c-2-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a kasra, heavy Dha says “ze”.",
      "title": "Dha (emphatic) with kasra",
      "ar": "ظِ",
      "aud": "c-3-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a damma, heavy Dha says “zo”.",
      "title": "Dha (emphatic) with damma",
      "ar": "ظُ",
      "aud": "c-4-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "“Memorization is a great blessing”",
      "title": "Sentence of the lesson",
      "ar": "الحِفْظُ نِعْمَةٌ عَظِيمَةٌ",
      "aud": "c-5-ar",
      "tr": "Al-Hifzu Ni'matun 'Azima"
    }
  ],
